gimmicks. So one of his gimmicks is he says to his cronies, never address me by my real name. Just call me the old man. It's like when Paul Inns, when he played for Manchester United, he insisted that people call him the governor. In this case, Stevenson insists that people call him the old man. He's a brilliant speaker, a rallies, doesn't know very well, and he turns the newsletter, the Fiery Cross into this weekly newspaper, and he recruited 9,000 paperboys to sell it across the Midwest. So is he the guy who's running that big festival that we began this episode with?
花招。所以他的花招之一是告诉他的亲信，永远不要用我的真名称呼我。只叫我“老人”。就像保罗·因斯在曼联踢球时，他坚持让人叫他“州长”。在这种情况下，史蒂文森坚持让人叫他“老人”。他是一位出色的演讲者，非常擅长集会，他把时事通讯《烈焰十字》变成了这份周报，并招募了9000名报童在整个中西部地区销售。那么他就是我们在本集开头提到的那个举办大型节日的人吗？

