There are obvious underlying reasons as well as the scandals. The clan's vision was much too negative. It had nothing positive to, you know, it was all about hatred of Catholics and stuff more than anything else. Apart from some Anodyne stuff about patriotism and family values, most of its appeal is based on negativity. Its vision of America is an outdated one. You know, America by the 1920s is clearly much. too diverse to be turned back into a white Protestant enclave. That's never going to happen. Also, I think most historians think it was a terrible mistake for the clan to enter mainstream politics. The clan's values of secrecy and exclusivity don't work in a democratic arena
除了丑闻之外，还有明显的潜在原因。三K党的愿景太消极了。它没有什么积极的东西，你知道，它更多的是关于对天主教徒的仇恨。除了关于爱国主义和家庭价值观的一些平淡的东西外，它的大部分吸引力都基于消极。它对美国的愿景是过时的。你知道，到1920年代，美国显然太多元化了，不可能变回白人新教徒的飞地。那永远不会发生。此外，我认为大多数历史学家认为三K党进入主流政治是一个可怕的错误。三K党的秘密和排他性价值观在民主舞台上行不通。

113
00:58:19.000 --> 00:59:05.000
where you have to make deals and compromises and you have to, you know, a pluralistic world in which you're appealing to bigotry and sectarianism. It doesn't work. There are some historians like Linda Gordon, who point out that actually maybe the clan stopped being so popular because it had actually won some of its battles. So the clan was always in favour of eugenics. And by the end of the 1920s, 30 American states had adopted eugenics laws with forced sterilization of criminals or people that were called defectives. And often the people who were singled out for this treatment tended to be very poor people or black people. So in other words, people that the clan didn't really like anyway. The clan also won the argument on immigration.
在多元化的世界里，你必须进行交易和妥协，而诉诸偏执和宗派主义是行不通的。一些历史学家，如琳达·戈登（Linda Gordon），指出三K党之所以不再那么受欢迎，可能是因为它已经赢得了一些斗争。三K党一直支持优生学。到20世纪20年代末，美国有30个州通过了优生学法律，对罪犯或所谓的“缺陷者”进行强制绝育。通常，被挑出来接受这种待遇的人往往是非常贫穷的人或黑人。换句话说，就是那些三K党本来就不喜欢的人。三K党在移民问题上也赢得了辩论。

114
00:59:05.000 --> 00:59:55.000
So in 1924, the Johnson Reed Act brought in immigration quotas that were based on an outdated census, the 1890 census. So basically an immigration regime that tried to turn about the clock because 70% of immigrants under this new legislation had to come from Britain, Germany or Ireland. In other words, let's try to recreate a 19th century white America. All immigration from Asia, for example, was banned under the new legislation, and southern and eastern European immigration was severely curtailed. And this regime lasted until the 50s. And partly as a result of this, anti-Catholicism as a force in American life basically began to dissipate. So, you know, the Pope's plot to attack the people of North Manchester on the northbound train.
因此，1924年的《约翰逊-里德法案》（Johnson-Reed Act）引入了基于过时人口普查（1890年人口普查）的移民配额。基本上，这是一个试图倒转时钟的移民制度，因为根据这项新立法，70%的移民必须来自英国、德国或爱尔兰。换句话说，让我们试着重塑一个19世纪的白人美国。例如，新立法禁止了所有来自亚洲的移民，并严重限制了来自南欧和东欧的移民。这种制度一直持续到50年代。部分由于这个原因，作为美国生活中一股力量的反天主教情绪基本上开始消散。所以，你知道，教皇袭击北曼彻斯特北行火车上人们的阴谋。

115
